Comment: Third-party Rust crates, exactly as published on crates.io, which
 the two Rust programs are built from (the source archive carries them so
 that the build needs no network). Each crate is in a directory of its own,
 name and version, with its licence text and copyright notices. The
 licence expressions that occur in the set are: MIT; Apache-2.0;
 "MIT OR Apache-2.0" and its variants, some also with Zlib, 0BSD or
 "Apache-2.0 WITH LLVM-exception" as further choices; "Unlicense OR MIT";
 Unicode-3.0 (the icu and related crates); Zlib (zlib-rs). Where a crate
 offers a choice, any of the offered licences may be used. The
 notices of the crates linked into the two programs are in
 /usr/share/doc/asus-zenbook-duo-ux8406-second-screen/THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES.txt and
 /usr/share/doc/asus-zenbook-duo-ux8406-tcc-guard/THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES.txt.
 .
 Only the crates' Rust sources are compiled; none of them is installed as
 a file of its own.

